# Line endings.
#
# Git stores text as LF and, on Windows, `core.autocrlf=true` hands the working
# tree CRLF. That is fine for Python — but `docker/Dockerfile` COPYs from the
# working tree, so a Windows checkout bakes CRLF shell scripts into a Linux
# image. The kernel then reads `#!/bin/sh\r`, looks for an interpreter literally
# named `sh\r`, and the container dies with the famously unhelpful
#
#     exec docker/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# Every worker/beat container was unstartable on a Windows checkout because of
# this. Pin the files that Linux has to execute.

*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
docker/entrypoint.sh text eol=lf

# Compiled catalogs are binary — never normalise, never diff as text.
*.mo binary
